            <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <airSeal>High level of air leakage. Many leaks have been observed coming from the building envelope, the equipment and the windows and doors.</airSeal>
                <mainWalls>The actual walls are estimated to be builted by 2x6 with a level of insulation estimated at R-20. This level of insulation doesn't meet the actual standards. We recommend the addition of insulation by the exterior to reach a level of R-40. This techique will contribute to seal the building properly and reduce the air leakage through the envelope.</mainWalls>
                <ceilingsCathedral>The actual roof insulation is estimated to be R-40, made by 2 layes of 6'' of batt inusulation with an individual level of insulation of R-20. The roof insulation doesn't meet the actual standard of R-60. We recoomend the addition of insulation to reach the standard.</ceilingsCathedral>
                <foundation>We recommend the addition of insulation.</foundation>
                <windows>The windows on the top floor have been changed recently, but the basement windows are the original. The original windows are wood windows. We recommend the replacement of tne wood windows by ENERGY STAR CERTIFIED product.</windows>
            </RURComments>
        </Options>
